Introduction to Geology — Perron and Jagoutz, MIT 12.001 (@geo-mit: 0, is #reference, #part-of @geo-sources) { r_423FFVY46CGEN2F2263F95KX6N
Taylor Perron and Oliver Jagoutz. Introduction to Geology, MIT 12.001, Fall 2013. [Official complete course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-001-introduction-to-geology-fall-2013/) · [Syllabus](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-001-introduction-to-geology-fall-2013/pages/syllabus/) · [Labs and exercises](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/12-001-introduction-to-geology-fall-2013/pages/labs-and-exercises/).

Work the full lecture-note, lab, exercise, and field-interpretation sequence. Published studies include mantle composition, mineral/rock identification, deformation, geochronology, plate boundaries, seismicity, stereonets, reading maps, and mapping. The field-trip material supports interpretation and preparation; following it online does not demonstrate practical field competence.

The campus syllabus uses Grotzinger and Jordan's commercial Understanding Earth, 2006, obtained separately. The open books here support the corresponding concepts. Preserve MIT OCW and specific third-party permission notices; the Rice plate-boundary activity has its own credited origin. Do not claim unprovided campus assessments or textbook contents are bundled. Course identity, syllabus, resource types, and public exercises checked on 29 October 2026. Media remain external.

